 	List of patch names (as arguments) to apply to this input. Patches are
 	defined at the top-level in the `Patches`_ section.
 
+Freshness shell
+--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+Input ``fresh-cmd`` optionally accepts ``shell="nu"``.
+Without it, commands run directly as argument vectors, as before. With it,
+Nixtamal renders the ``$`` command and subsequent ``|`` stages as a pipeline
+and invokes the named executable with ``-c`` and that script. ``shell`` is a
+single executable name or path, not an executable plus command-line options.
+Nushell is invoked with ``--no-config-file``; other shells use POSIX argument
+quoting and must accept ``-c``.
+
+.. code-block:: text
+
+	fresh-cmd shell="nu" {
+		$ http get "https://api.github.com/repos/OWNER/REPO/releases/latest"
+		| get tag_name
+	}
+
+Arguments, including template substitutions, remain literal data. This is not
+a raw script-fragment interface: shell operators, variable expansion and
+redirections inside an argument are quoted, not evaluated. Nu command words,
+subcommands and flags remain recognizable; strings requiring quoting are
+escaped for Nu rather than POSIX shell syntax. Integer and decimal tokens with
+a duration or filesize unit (``30sec``, ``1.5min``, ``512mib``) remain bare so
+Nushell parses them as measures, not strings. Use separate flag and value
+arguments for Nu builtins. Pipeline exit behavior is the selected shell's;
+Nixtamal still rejects a nonzero shell exit or an empty freshness result.
+The shared codec also preserves this attribute on remote patch definitions,
+but the pinned upstream does not execute their freshness commands; this patch
+does not add that separate refresh behaviour.
+
 File
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
